## Case (ck.db AWPTCM-T22653, folder /Modbus/Proj 2166 Modbus Support)
Objective: able to retrieve port information. Steps (each "Confirm this is same as CLI"):
1 read 0x5000 #1 Port Current State (R, 1 word HEX); 2 read 0x5001 #1 Port Configured State
(RW, 1 word HEX); 3 read 0x5002 #1 Port PoE Configuration (RW, HEX); 4 read 0x5003 #1 Port PoE
Data Pairs Current Power Usage (R, UINT); 5 read 0x5004 #1 Port PoE Spare Pairs Current Power
Usage (R, UINT); 6 read 0x5005 #1 Port Input Bytes (R, 4 words UINT); 7 read 0x5009 #1 Port
Output Bytes (R, 4 words UINT).
Register semantics (ART suite raw-data/testsuites_art/1359_modbus/library_1359.py, the same
map): port state word = 4 nibbles [state, duplex, polarity, speed]: state 0=down F=up; duplex
0=auto 1=full 2=half; polarity 0=auto 1=mdi 2=mdix; speed 0=auto 1=10 2=100 3=1000 4=10000
5=40000 6=100000. Ports are 13 words each from 0x5000, in port order per stack member, and the
per-member blocks are addressed by Modbus UNIT ID = stack member number (ART: unit=member).
"#1 port" = the first port of member 1 = port1.0.1 (an empty SFP cage on this bench, link down).

